{
  title: "237 a thunk in a list literal is shared across forces"
  doc: "eu-oaz72.48: forcing a list element that refers to a let-bound thunk
        outside the list's own frame must update that thunk, not a copy of
        it. The tick gate is in `tests/harness_test.rs`, which runs both
        targets with demand analysis suppressed (so no strictness rewrite
        hides the defect) and requires `shared` to cost about one fold."
}

m: range(0, 20000) count
x: [m]

` "the target computes the right value"
passes(context): (context.result.ok) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

` { target: :fold
    verify: [:passes] }
fold: {
  ok: m = 20000
}

# Three forces of the element: one fold if the thunk is shared, three if
# each force recomputes it from a copy.
` { target: :shared
    verify: [:passes] }
shared: {
  y: [x first, x first, x first]
  ok: y = [20000, 20000, 20000]
}
